## qf-lit2 | Quick-fire: books 2 | lit | 0 | - | qf-lit
quiz 2 | Who wrote Pride and Prejudice?
* Jane Austen
o Charlotte Brontë
o George Eliot
o Mary Shelley
= 1813.
> Next

quiz 2 | Who wrote The Odyssey?
* Homer (traditionally)
o Virgil
o Sophocles
o Ovid
= Composed around the 8th century BC, likely from an oral tradition.
> Next

quiz 3 | Who wrote To Kill a Mockingbird?
* Harper Lee
o John Steinbeck
o Truman Capote
o William Faulkner
= 1960. Capote was her childhood friend and inspired the character Dill.
> Next

quiz 3 | Who wrote The Catcher in the Rye?
* J. D. Salinger
o Jack Kerouac
o Ernest Hemingway
o Kurt Vonnegut
= 1951, narrated by Holden Caulfield.
> Next

quiz 3 | Which Brontë sister wrote Wuthering Heights?
* Emily
o Charlotte
o Anne
= Published in 1847 under the name Ellis Bell.
> Next

quiz 3 | Who wrote The Trial and The Castle?
* Franz Kafka
o Thomas Mann
o Hermann Hesse
o Robert Musil
= Both published after his death by Max Brod.
> Next

quiz 3 | Who wrote Things Fall Apart (1958)?
* Chinua Achebe
o Wole Soyinka
o Ngũgĩ wa Thiong'o
o Ben Okri
= One of the most widely read African novels.
> Next

quiz 4 | Who wrote Slaughterhouse-Five?
* Kurt Vonnegut
o Joseph Heller
o Norman Mailer
o Philip Roth
= Vonnegut survived the bombing of Dresden as a prisoner of war in a meat locker.
> Next

quiz 4 | Who wrote The Brothers Karamazov?
* Fyodor Dostoevsky
o Leo Tolstoy
o Ivan Turgenev
o Nikolai Gogol
= His final novel, 1880.
> Next

quiz 4 | Which poet wrote "The Road Not Taken"?
* Robert Frost
o Walt Whitman
o Emily Dickinson
o T. S. Eliot
= Often read as advice to be bold; Frost said it was a gentle joke about a friend's indecision.
