quiz 2 | Which is the smallest country in the world?
* Vatican City
o Monaco
o San Marino
o Liechtenstein
= About 0.44 km².
> Next

quiz 3 | Which country has the largest population (as of the mid-2020s)?
* India
o China
o USA
o Indonesia
= India passed China in 2023.
> Next

quiz 3 | Mount Kilimanjaro is in…
* Tanzania
o Kenya
o Uganda
o Ethiopia
= Africa's highest peak, at about 5,895 m.
> Next

quiz 3 | Which country is both in Europe and Asia?
* Turkey
o Greece
o Egypt
o Iran
= Istanbul straddles the Bosphorus. Russia and Kazakhstan do too.
> Next

quiz 3 | What's the capital of Canada?
* Ottawa
o Toronto
o Montreal
o Vancouver
= Chosen by Queen Victoria in 1857.
> Next

quiz 4 | Which line divides the Earth into Northern and Southern Hemispheres?
* The equator
o The Prime Meridian
o The Tropic of Cancer
o The International Date Line
= The Prime Meridian divides east and west.
> Next

quiz 4 | Which country has the most islands?
* Sweden (by most counts)
o Indonesia
o Philippines
o Japan
= About 267,000 islands, most tiny and uninhabited.
> Next

quiz 4 | Which is the highest capital city?
* La Paz, Bolivia (seat of government)
o Quito
o Kathmandu
o Bogotá
= About 3,600 m. Sucre is Bolivia's constitutional capital.
> Next

quiz 4 | The Sahara is roughly the size of…
* The USA (or China)
o France
o The UK
o Australia ×3
= About 9 million km².
