## qf-math3 | Quick-fire: maths 3 | maths | 1 | - | qf-maths2
quiz 3 | How many prime numbers are there below 20?
* 8
o 7
o 9
o 10
= 2, 3, 5, 7, 11, 13, 17, 19.
> Next

quiz 3 | Perimeter of a semicircle of radius 1 (including the diameter)?
* π + 2
o π
o 2π
o 2π + 2
= Curved part π, plus the straight diameter 2.
> Next

quiz 3 | What is 7! / 5!?
* 42
o 2
o 35
o 5,040
= 7 × 6.
> Next

quiz 4 | Probability that a random integer is divisible by 2 or 3?
* 2/3
o 5/6
o 1/2
o 1/6
= 1/2 + 1/3 − 1/6.
> Next

quiz 4 | What's the next term: 1, 1, 2, 3, 5, 8, 13, …?
* 21
o 18
o 20
o 26
= Fibonacci: add the previous two.
> Next

quiz 4 | How many subsets does a set with 5 elements have?
* 32
o 25
o 10
o 120
= 2⁵: each element is in or out.
> Next

quiz 4 | What's the angle sum of a triangle drawn on a sphere?
* More than 180°
o Exactly 180°
o Less than 180°
o 360°
= A triangle from the North Pole to two points on the equator 90° apart has three right angles: 270°.
> Next

quiz 4 | How many handshakes if 10 people each shake hands once with everyone else?
* 45
o 100
o 90
o 10
= 10C2.
> Next

quiz 4 | What's the probability of drawing two aces from a deck (without replacement)?
* 1/221
o 1/169
o 1/52
o 1/26
= (4/52) × (3/51).
> Next

quiz 5 | Which is larger: 100! or 100¹⁰⁰?
* 100¹⁰⁰
o 100!
o They're equal
= 100! multiplies 100 numbers that are mostly less than 100.
> Quick-fire round seven complete
